>> title: Beef Stew
>> servings: 8
>> source: https://www.delish.com/cooking/recipe-ideas/a23515497/easy-beef-stew-recipe/

Heat @vegetable oil{1%tbsp} in a large #Dutch oven{} or heavy pot over medium heat. Add @beef chuck stew meat{2%lb}(cut into 1" cubes) and cook, turning occasionally, until seared on all sides, about ~{10%minutes}. Transfer beef to a plate.

Coat the bottom of the pot with oil if needed and heat over medium-high heat. Cook @onion{1}(chopped), @carrots{2}(peeled and cut into rounds), and @celery{2 stalks}(chopped), stirring occasionally, until softened, about ~{7%minutes}; season with @salt{} and @black pepper{}. 

Add @garlic{3%cloves}(finely chopped) and @tomato paste{0.25%cups} and cook, stirring, until garlic is fragrant and tomato paste is darkened, about ~{2%minutes}. 

Return beef and any accumulated juices to the pot. Add @beef broth{6%cups}, @red wine{1%cups}, @Worcestershire sauce{1%tbsp}, @thyme{2 sprigs}, and @bay leaves{2}. Bring to a boil, then reduce heat to medium-low and bring to a simmer; season with @salt{} and @black pepper{}. Cover and simmer, stirring occasionally, until beef is tender, ~{30-45%minutes}.

Add @baby potatoes{1%lb}(halved) and simmer, covered, until potatoes are tender, about ~{15%minutes}.

Remove @bay leaves{} and @thyme{}. Stir in @frozen peas{1%c} and cook, stirring, until warmed through, about ~{2%minutes}; season with @salt{} and @black pepper{}.

Divide stew among bowls. Top with @parsley{}(chopped).